Fix: toolbar placement for Windowed/horizontal overlays and minimum Windowed height

- Rename the existing working folder to changes/windowed-toolbar-layout/windowed-toolbar-layout/ before making feature changes; preserve all existing files and icon blobs.
- Move whichever toolbar button occupies the vertical overlay's bottom edge slot inline to the right of the other two toolbar buttons in Windowed mode and horizontal docked mode.
- Recalculate toolbar placement when the layout mode changes, including transitions into or out of Windowed mode and changes to the configured edge button.
- Reduce the horizontal overlay's inline search field to 88 CSS pixels so the “Search” placeholder remains visible without the oversized field.
- Enforce a minimum Windowed height of 35% of screen height in the initial geometry, normal geometry application, and interactive resizing; cap that minimum only if the browser viewport cannot fit it.
- Keep existing toolbar order and the selected edge-button identity intact.
